## Adopt a workspace

A workspace is created by a person signing up in the web app. Bring it under Terraform with an `import` block that names its slug, next to a `spotlight_workspace` whose `name` and `slug` match what is there, so the first plan imports it and changes nothing. Terraform then manages everything inside it: its teams, lines, skills, integrations and harness profiles, its secrets, and its runner pools and trusts.

{{ tffile .ExampleFile }}

## Creating a workspace

Creating a workspace from Terraform needs a caller allowed to open workspaces. API tokens are not: a token acts only inside its own workspace, and opening one is refused with `403 Forbidden`. The provider reports that refusal with the `import` block to write instead.

## Stop managing a workspace

Destroying a `spotlight_workspace` asks Spotlight to delete the workspace. To stop managing it without deleting it, replace the resource with a `removed` block (Terraform 1.7 or later):

{{ tffile "examples/resources/spotlight_workspace/removed.tf" }}

